1
00:00:21,292 --> 00:00:23,669
Feeling a lil' antsy there, Julio?

2
00:00:23,753 --> 00:00:24,879
No way!

3
00:00:25,671 --> 00:00:28,174
You're the one Wakako sicced on us, right?

4
00:00:28,257 --> 00:00:29,800
Heard you're David's fan.

5
00:00:29,884 --> 00:00:32,553
Yeah! But what do you mean
she sicced me on you?

6
00:00:32,636 --> 00:00:34,889
Hear that, David?

7
00:00:35,473 --> 00:00:39,060
You have fans now.
Probably 'cause you got all swole.

8
00:00:39,852 --> 00:00:40,895
Where's your gun?

9
00:00:41,687 --> 00:00:42,938
What do you use?

10
00:00:43,022 --> 00:00:44,732
Uh, I've got a Lexington.

11
00:00:44,815 --> 00:00:46,525
That won't cut it.

12
00:00:46,609 --> 00:00:49,528
You gonna go up
against Maelstrom with that?

13
00:00:50,112 --> 00:00:51,030
Use this.

14
00:00:51,989 --> 00:00:54,450
Seriously, dude?! A fucking Satara!

15
00:00:54,533 --> 00:00:56,160
Nova! Thanks, man!

16
00:00:56,744 --> 00:00:59,580
Tech shotguns are so cool.

17
00:01:00,331 --> 00:01:02,124
Charge-up shots, oh yeah…

18
00:01:03,042 --> 00:01:04,085
Boom!

19
00:01:05,127 --> 00:01:06,295
Boom!

20
00:01:07,296 --> 00:01:08,172
Boom!

21
00:01:08,255 --> 00:01:10,508
Knock it off!

22
00:01:10,591 --> 00:01:12,343
Ow! Stop! Watch the knees!

23
00:01:12,426 --> 00:01:14,804
What are you, five?!

24
00:01:14,887 --> 00:01:17,932
Just stick behind me. Don't rush ahead.

25
00:01:18,015 --> 00:01:22,061
You want me to take rear?
I ain't no rookie, man.

26
00:01:22,770 --> 00:01:23,687
Attention, ladies.

27
00:01:24,271 --> 00:01:25,940
One minute from the destination.

28
00:03:21,013 --> 00:03:23,015
Looks like they're heading in the front.

29
00:03:23,098 --> 00:03:25,017
Clearly. Meatbrain move!

30
00:03:26,477 --> 00:03:27,561
The fuck?

31
00:03:28,187 --> 00:03:30,022
Who ordered lunch meat?

32
00:03:30,105 --> 00:03:32,274
Ya little babies lost?

33
00:03:32,358 --> 00:03:34,777
Looks like they wanna start something.

34
00:03:34,860 --> 00:03:37,279
You got shit in your ears?!

35
00:03:37,863 --> 00:03:41,867
Better start talking before
I drill you a fresh earhole--

36
00:03:41,951 --> 00:03:43,786
Better stop talking before you die.

37
00:03:49,041 --> 00:03:51,543
Tagging complete. Short circ incoming…

38
00:03:52,169 --> 00:03:54,797
Done! Close-call but made it, asshole!

39
00:03:55,422 --> 00:03:57,800
Fuck! They've got a netrunner!

40
00:04:06,016 --> 00:04:08,185
Ahh! We're all gonna die!

41
00:04:10,646 --> 00:04:13,065
Come on!

42
00:04:13,983 --> 00:04:15,109
Out of ammo!

43
00:04:15,192 --> 00:04:16,986
Bitch got no juice!

44
00:04:17,069 --> 00:04:18,112
Fuck her up!

45
00:04:18,195 --> 00:04:21,031
Time for… the big guns!

46
00:04:23,242 --> 00:04:24,118
There's a turret!

47
00:04:27,204 --> 00:04:29,373
Watch out! The runner's got control of--

48
00:04:29,456 --> 00:04:32,376
Damn brat, ordering me around…

49
00:04:42,511 --> 00:04:46,640
Ready to play with a real Maelstrom?

50
00:04:46,724 --> 00:04:47,766
Oh, damn…

51
00:04:47,850 --> 00:04:50,644
That shit even human?!

52
00:04:59,695 --> 00:05:02,906
Gimme that organic ass…

53
00:05:13,751 --> 00:05:18,005
And I'll tear you a new hole!

54
00:05:29,475 --> 00:05:32,978
You're the one getting a new hole.

55
00:05:38,317 --> 00:05:40,986
That was insane! …Zoot-zoot-zoot, bang!

56
00:05:41,070 --> 00:05:44,239
Those your new leg implants? Looking good.

57
00:05:51,705 --> 00:05:53,665
Got it! Room in the back, right?

58
00:05:53,749 --> 00:05:54,750
Wait! Julio!

59
00:05:54,833 --> 00:05:56,001
If there are traps…

60
00:06:08,972 --> 00:06:10,891
Isabella Morgan, where you at?

61
00:06:12,976 --> 00:06:15,145
Your dad put out an SOS for you.

62
00:06:15,729 --> 00:06:17,064
You're safe now.

63
00:07:03,318 --> 00:07:04,444
Thank ya kindly.

64
00:07:05,195 --> 00:07:07,447
Thanks for taking the wheel, Falco.

65
00:07:07,531 --> 00:07:09,908
No sweat off my back.

66
00:07:10,450 --> 00:07:13,537
Nah, good drivers are hard to come by.

67
00:07:13,620 --> 00:07:17,249
Dunno about that.
Seems you got a fan club now.

68
00:07:17,332 --> 00:07:18,959
You mean like Julio?

69
00:07:19,042 --> 00:07:22,588
I knew that gonk was bluffing
the moment I saw him.

70
00:07:24,214 --> 00:07:30,262
Aren't many veterans who'd work with
a kid like me unless they knew Maine.

71
00:07:30,345 --> 00:07:33,432
Gotta admit, first time you called,

72
00:07:33,515 --> 00:07:36,268
I thought you were a pushy pipsqueak.

73
00:07:39,396 --> 00:07:41,732
But now? Well…

74
00:07:42,441 --> 00:07:44,985
You're gonna go further
than Maine ever could.

75
00:07:47,821 --> 00:07:50,282
Gonna roll out before this gets all sappy.

76
00:07:50,365 --> 00:07:52,493
Buzz me for your next big gig, huh?

77
00:07:52,576 --> 00:07:55,329
Catch you later, David. Kiwi.

78
00:07:55,412 --> 00:07:56,246
See ya.

79
00:07:56,830 --> 00:07:57,998
Bye.

80
00:08:00,167 --> 00:08:04,254
Honestly? I doubted you had it
in you to take the reins.

81
00:08:04,338 --> 00:08:07,049
All thanks to our preem runner.

82
00:08:07,132 --> 00:08:11,094
We both know you don't mean me.

83
00:08:12,638 --> 00:08:14,348
You've asked her, right?

84
00:08:15,015 --> 00:08:18,560
Used to. I kinda gave up trying.

85
00:08:18,644 --> 00:08:22,564
Didn't peg her as the type
to get cold feet.

86
00:08:22,648 --> 00:08:26,777
I bet it's more than
what happened to Maine and Dorio.

87
00:08:27,444 --> 00:08:31,865
Back at the warehouse,
Lucy was acting weird.

88
00:08:31,949 --> 00:08:33,158
Meaning what?

89
00:08:33,242 --> 00:08:36,870
Whole thing's kind of a blur.
Might've been nothing.

90
00:08:39,873 --> 00:08:45,629
Speaking of, you're the one
that brought Lucy into the crew, right?

91
00:08:45,712 --> 00:08:46,797
Yeah.

92
00:08:46,880 --> 00:08:49,132
She talk to you about her past?

93
00:08:49,216 --> 00:08:50,676
Nope.

94
00:08:51,385 --> 00:08:55,639
Most of the saps in our league
don't bring up the old days.

95
00:08:55,722 --> 00:08:59,268
Shame, greed,
something to prove… whatever.

96
00:08:59,351 --> 00:09:02,521
Whether you're looking for a way out
or a way up, does it matter?

97
00:09:06,108 --> 00:09:07,818
Why the long face, David?!

98
00:09:07,901 --> 00:09:11,405
Stop flirting with the nagging hag
and dance with me!

99
00:09:12,573 --> 00:09:17,035
Although some edgerunners die
in more shame than they started with…

100
00:09:17,119 --> 00:09:23,166
At least I didn't get flatlined
by a psycho with his dick out in the wind.

101
00:09:23,250 --> 00:09:27,546
Anyway, have you ever seen
David dance? It's a riot…

102
00:09:27,629 --> 00:09:31,174
Sorry, I'm heading out.
Gonna stop by Doc's.

103
00:09:31,258 --> 00:09:33,051
Wha? Again?

104
00:09:33,135 --> 00:09:36,054
Tell him to sell you
a dance chip or something!

105
00:09:36,138 --> 00:09:37,556
-A real good one!
-Shut up.

106
00:09:37,639 --> 00:09:38,849
Catch ya later.

107
00:09:41,310 --> 00:09:44,730
Why you gotta play
hard-to-get all the time?!

108
00:09:44,813 --> 00:09:47,149
Why don't you shake up your approach?

109
00:09:47,232 --> 00:09:48,567
Yeah?

110
00:09:49,318 --> 00:09:53,155
Think I should play shy and nerdy…
at the shy and nerdy?

111
00:09:57,159 --> 00:10:01,246
This warped piece of metal's just
shoved up your arm socket.

112
00:10:01,330 --> 00:10:03,582
It doesn't fit you in the first place.

113
00:10:04,416 --> 00:10:06,501
On top of that, it's an old model.

114
00:10:06,585 --> 00:10:09,338
Got all kinds of next-gen chrome out back…

115
00:10:09,421 --> 00:10:11,340
I'm fine with this one.

116
00:10:11,423 --> 00:10:14,843
Tsk. Fine. It's your funeral.

117
00:10:14,926 --> 00:10:19,139
Got muscle reinforcers?
Kiroshi's new model?

118
00:10:19,222 --> 00:10:22,392
Didn't know I was talking to
a tweaked out chromehead.

119
00:10:22,476 --> 00:10:23,602
I'm not.

120
00:10:24,186 --> 00:10:25,687
You need to take it easy.

121
00:10:25,771 --> 00:10:28,649
At this rate, ain't no way
your mind can keep up.

122
00:10:28,732 --> 00:10:30,067
I'm fine.

123
00:10:30,150 --> 00:10:33,695
No matter how much chrome I get,
I don't feel a damn thing.

124
00:10:33,779 --> 00:10:36,448
Metal feels better
than being in my own skin.

125
00:10:36,531 --> 00:10:40,619
Gotta admit, your adaptability to
cyberware is fucking nuts.

126
00:10:40,702 --> 00:10:44,122
Ain't never seen a kid
cyborg out quite like this.

127
00:10:44,206 --> 00:10:46,833
Your cyberware capacity's already--

128
00:10:46,917 --> 00:10:49,002
You think you're special?

129
00:10:49,086 --> 00:10:51,421
Just must be special, I guess.

130
00:10:52,422 --> 00:10:54,800
You aiming to be like
Adam Smasher or what?

131
00:10:54,883 --> 00:10:56,051
Adam what?

132
00:10:56,134 --> 00:10:58,929
Damn. All this time and
you're still a fucking newb.

133
00:10:59,012 --> 00:11:01,682
Don't even know Adam Smasher.

134
00:11:01,765 --> 00:11:04,851
Some know him as a war hero
from the 4th Corporate War.

135
00:11:04,935 --> 00:11:09,189
To others, a fully cyborged
boogeyman, walking nightmare.

136
00:11:09,272 --> 00:11:13,318
But to all, a living legend, ask anyone.

137
00:11:13,902 --> 00:11:15,654
What kinda legend?

138
00:11:15,737 --> 00:11:17,823
There's probably a graveyard out there

139
00:11:17,906 --> 00:11:20,492
full of big shots he flatlined
on Arasaka's orders.

140
00:11:20,575 --> 00:11:22,285
Sounds like a hoax.

141
00:11:23,662 --> 00:11:24,830
Kiwi?

142
00:11:26,164 --> 00:11:27,124
What's up?

143
00:11:27,207 --> 00:11:30,085
Can you drop by the Afterlife?

144
00:11:30,168 --> 00:11:32,587
You guys still out bar hopping?

145
00:11:32,671 --> 00:11:35,090
Got someone here who wants to see you.

146
00:11:35,715 --> 00:11:36,758
David.

147
00:11:36,842 --> 00:11:38,969
Hey, Kiwi.

148
00:11:39,886 --> 00:11:41,096
Wish you luck.

149
00:11:43,598 --> 00:11:47,102
I believe this is the first time
we meet, Mister Martinez.

150
00:11:47,185 --> 00:11:50,605
We've crossed paths…
You came to a party once to talk to Maine.

151
00:11:51,815 --> 00:11:55,110
Is that so?
I believe introductions are in order.

152
00:11:55,193 --> 00:11:56,486
I am Faraday.

153
00:11:59,614 --> 00:12:01,158
You have a job for me?

154
00:12:01,241 --> 00:12:04,995
No need to rush. Let me buy you a drink.

155
00:12:05,620 --> 00:12:08,874
I've heard a great deal about you.

156
00:12:09,458 --> 00:12:12,419
You are making quite a name for yourself.

157
00:12:12,502 --> 00:12:14,880
The rookie with the Sandevistan.

158
00:12:15,464 --> 00:12:18,091
I've got more than the Sandy now.

159
00:12:18,175 --> 00:12:22,137
This is true. It seems now
you are more steel than bone.

160
00:12:22,888 --> 00:12:26,183
Maine and I had
a mutually beneficial work relationship.

161
00:12:26,266 --> 00:12:27,601
I know.

162
00:12:27,684 --> 00:12:30,312
He understood crew chemistry.

163
00:12:30,395 --> 00:12:31,229
He did.

164
00:12:31,313 --> 00:12:35,150
But his flaw was personal attachment.

165
00:12:35,233 --> 00:12:37,652
Familiarity muddies the mind,
leads to ruin.

166
00:12:39,237 --> 00:12:41,990
I hear that you're also good
with teamwork.

167
00:12:42,073 --> 00:12:44,826
But I keep my private
and professional life separate.

168
00:12:44,910 --> 00:12:49,873
I would like for you to convince me that
you can work at the same level as Maine.

169
00:12:49,956 --> 00:12:50,999
You're testing me?

170
00:12:51,082 --> 00:12:53,335
You can think of it that way.

171
00:12:53,418 --> 00:12:56,671
You can test me all you want,
but I ain't running jobs for cheap.

172
00:12:56,755 --> 00:12:59,174
Nothing I do is cheap.

173
00:13:06,890 --> 00:13:08,808
This a Militech job?

174
00:13:08,892 --> 00:13:11,061
They're at odds with Arasaka.

175
00:13:11,144 --> 00:13:15,315
As you might expect,
corporate jobs pay out the most.

176
00:13:15,398 --> 00:13:17,526
Do you oppose?

177
00:13:18,652 --> 00:13:19,653
Consider it done.

178
00:13:19,736 --> 00:13:21,071
Good to hear.

179
00:13:21,154 --> 00:13:24,908
There is an assignment
I'd like you to take over after this job.

180
00:13:24,991 --> 00:13:26,535
It's a matter familiar to you.

181
00:13:26,618 --> 00:13:29,037
You mean the data you wanted from Tanaka?

182
00:13:29,120 --> 00:13:33,250
Unfortunately, I received a report
that Tanaka had no data.

183
00:13:33,333 --> 00:13:34,167
Yup.

184
00:13:34,251 --> 00:13:38,129
But I also received a report that
you successfully bypassed Arasaka's ICE.

185
00:13:38,213 --> 00:13:42,050
And that this wasn't done by Kiwi,
but by a back-up runner.

186
00:13:42,133 --> 00:13:45,470
Yeah. Our team's got
lucky with good runners.

187
00:13:45,554 --> 00:13:48,557
Excellent. However, I hear
this runner is not present.

188
00:13:49,140 --> 00:13:52,060
Yeah. They left the team after that case.

189
00:13:52,143 --> 00:13:55,564
Why is that? Such a waste of good talent.

190
00:13:56,147 --> 00:13:57,816
Their heart's just not in it.

191
00:13:57,899 --> 00:14:01,069
It wouldn't hurt to try
to convince her again.

192
00:14:01,152 --> 00:14:03,029
Easier said than done…

193
00:14:06,032 --> 00:14:09,452
Arasaka knows that
Militech's after them, right?

194
00:14:09,536 --> 00:14:11,037
Of course.

195
00:14:11,121 --> 00:14:13,832
What's Militech after
that they'd want this bad?

196
00:14:14,416 --> 00:14:18,211
That is my concern and none of yours.

197
00:14:18,795 --> 00:14:20,964
Needless details
would only get in your way.

198
00:14:21,798 --> 00:14:23,717
Learn anything new that might help?

199
00:14:23,800 --> 00:14:27,721
Not yet. But as they say,
"Good things come to those who wait."

200
00:14:28,305 --> 00:14:31,349
But you've yet to prove
that you're worth my time.

201
00:14:41,776 --> 00:14:42,611
You're home.

202
00:14:46,197 --> 00:14:47,782
It's pretty late.

203
00:14:49,200 --> 00:14:51,536
Got caught up.

204
00:14:51,620 --> 00:14:53,455
Made a victory lap at Minjung's?

205
00:14:53,538 --> 00:14:54,456
Yeah.

206
00:14:54,539 --> 00:14:56,082
Any problems on the job?

207
00:14:56,166 --> 00:14:58,168
We lost someone tonight.

208
00:14:58,710 --> 00:15:00,003
Who?

209
00:15:00,086 --> 00:15:02,380
Greenhorn solo Wakako sent us.

210
00:15:02,464 --> 00:15:05,425
Oh. But everything went fine otherwise?

211
00:15:05,508 --> 00:15:08,428
Easy. The newb just jumped the gun.

212
00:15:08,929 --> 00:15:11,222
Sounds like some other newb I once knew.

213
00:15:11,306 --> 00:15:12,390
Hey.

214
00:15:14,851 --> 00:15:15,852
So…

215
00:15:16,728 --> 00:15:19,022
We got something big coming up.

216
00:15:19,105 --> 00:15:20,649
How fun.

217
00:15:20,732 --> 00:15:24,194
And it'd really help
if you'd get on board…

218
00:15:24,277 --> 00:15:27,405
Two runners makes for a crowd, doesn't it?

219
00:15:27,489 --> 00:15:30,492
You know that I'd rather have--

220
00:15:30,575 --> 00:15:31,826
David, please.

221
00:15:33,036 --> 00:15:34,913
I need more time.

222
00:15:36,748 --> 00:15:38,917
Fine. Okay.

223
00:15:40,460 --> 00:15:41,878
You were diving again?

224
00:15:43,213 --> 00:15:45,465
Why don't you buy a runnersuit?

225
00:15:45,548 --> 00:15:46,883
Don't need one.

226
00:15:46,967 --> 00:15:51,388
We can get you a new chair.
The ice-bath can't be comfortable.

227
00:15:52,055 --> 00:15:55,100
Thank you.
But I don't like wearing a suit.

228
00:15:55,767 --> 00:15:56,685
Oh.

229
00:15:56,768 --> 00:15:58,728
Sorry, I didn't know.

230
00:16:03,274 --> 00:16:04,859
Hey, David?

231
00:16:06,277 --> 00:16:07,153
Come with me.

232
00:16:14,786 --> 00:16:17,288
Whoa! Look at the stars!

233
00:16:17,372 --> 00:16:19,749
Can't get a view like this in the city.

234
00:16:20,709 --> 00:16:22,836
-Think I can catch one?
-As if.

235
00:16:23,420 --> 00:16:25,380
Wish we could've seen the moon.

236
00:16:25,463 --> 00:16:28,383
The stars shine brighter
because the moon's not out.

237
00:16:28,466 --> 00:16:29,551
Really?

238
00:16:29,634 --> 00:16:32,512
The moon outshines the stars.

239
00:16:32,595 --> 00:16:34,764
What were they teaching you
at the Academy?

240
00:16:34,848 --> 00:16:36,474
I'm a drop-out, remember?

241
00:16:36,558 --> 00:16:38,101
Right, right.

242
00:16:38,184 --> 00:16:41,688
Never been outside of the city.

243
00:16:42,188 --> 00:16:43,106
Huh.

244
00:16:44,274 --> 00:16:47,360
You had a life outside the city once, huh?

245
00:16:50,530 --> 00:16:54,743
The city looks like a cage
made of lights from here.

246
00:16:57,704 --> 00:16:59,122
You may not remember…

247
00:17:01,082 --> 00:17:04,002
You said you and I are different.

248
00:17:04,794 --> 00:17:05,628
Yes.

249
00:17:06,171 --> 00:17:08,298
What did you mean by that?

250
00:17:10,842 --> 00:17:12,302
Don't wanna talk about it?

251
00:17:14,888 --> 00:17:16,431
You'd rather not hear.

252
00:17:16,514 --> 00:17:19,768
I just… wanna know more about you.

253
00:17:24,355 --> 00:17:25,523
Arasaka.

254
00:17:25,607 --> 00:17:26,649
Arasaka?

255
00:17:26,733 --> 00:17:27,901
Yes.

256
00:17:27,984 --> 00:17:32,030
I was born in a different country
and raised in an Arasaka facility.

257
00:17:32,822 --> 00:17:38,536
Including me, 13 children passed
proficiency tests to become netrunners.

258
00:17:39,454 --> 00:17:42,290
Kids who wouldn't be missed
if they disappeared.

259
00:17:42,373 --> 00:17:45,960
"We'll serve the world's most
powerful megacorp one day…"

260
00:17:46,044 --> 00:17:50,757
That dream is what got us through
the hard days of training.

261
00:17:51,382 --> 00:17:55,887
It's the dream we were given,
the dream we never questioned.

262
00:17:56,888 --> 00:18:01,893
But when training ended,
we weren't assigned to a corpo office.

263
00:18:02,685 --> 00:18:08,024
We were taken to an underground facility
where we were constantly forced to dive…

264
00:18:08,108 --> 00:18:12,237
They sent us into the Old Net.

265
00:18:12,320 --> 00:18:14,280
Old Net?

266
00:18:14,364 --> 00:18:18,701
That's the old internet domain that
collapsed around 50 years ago, right?

267
00:18:18,785 --> 00:18:19,619
Yes.

268
00:18:19,702 --> 00:18:22,747
Brought down by history's greatest
netrunner, creator of daemons…

269
00:18:22,831 --> 00:18:27,043
Hacker savant, legend, Rache Bartmoss.

270
00:18:27,127 --> 00:18:32,757
The guy that brought down
78 percent of the world wide web.

271
00:18:32,841 --> 00:18:37,387
His DataKrash virus shattered cyberspace…

272
00:18:37,470 --> 00:18:43,601
…Broke the Net into a scattered
mosaic of isolated localnets.

273
00:18:44,602 --> 00:18:49,232
Arasaka's purpose was in the Old Net.
The legacies of the past.

274
00:18:49,315 --> 00:18:51,568
Vast amounts of lost knowledge.

275
00:18:51,651 --> 00:18:57,198
And we were soldiers being sent to a nest
of illegal malware and aggressive AI.

276
00:18:58,116 --> 00:19:02,203
Advanced netrunners can dive
into it with their whole mind.

277
00:19:02,287 --> 00:19:03,705
You mean deep-diving.

278
00:19:03,788 --> 00:19:06,791
And diving materializes cyberspace
into a traversable world.

279
00:19:06,875 --> 00:19:11,337
But whenever we uncovered
any rare data cache…

280
00:19:15,300 --> 00:19:19,179
Rogue AIs would find and attack us.

281
00:19:19,929 --> 00:19:22,682
We were picked off one by one.

282
00:19:23,641 --> 00:19:27,937
I continued to dive,
thinking that each time would be my last.

283
00:19:28,646 --> 00:19:31,983
Soon, there were only
a handful of us left.

284
00:19:32,692 --> 00:19:37,113
We were being killed
to live someone else's dream.

285
00:19:37,197 --> 00:19:41,701
So we thought, "If we're going to die,
why not die trying to escape?"

286
00:19:43,369 --> 00:19:47,457
The tech staff didn't stand a chance.
Not against the skills they'd taught us.

287
00:19:48,166 --> 00:19:49,500
And we escaped.

288
00:19:58,551 --> 00:20:00,470
I kept running.

289
00:20:00,553 --> 00:20:03,139
I could hear my friends crying out,

290
00:20:03,223 --> 00:20:05,099
but I didn't look back.

291
00:20:13,066 --> 00:20:17,028
When I came to,
I was living out in a junkyard.

292
00:20:17,570 --> 00:20:21,366
After that, I was too scared
to stay in one place.

293
00:20:21,449 --> 00:20:23,534
So I traveled to different cities.

294
00:20:25,912 --> 00:20:29,499
But there's no place like Night City
if all you wanna do is hide.

295
00:20:29,582 --> 00:20:32,502
You still feel like you're being chased?

296
00:20:33,127 --> 00:20:37,257
Not really. Guess I just got
too comfortable here.

297
00:20:37,840 --> 00:20:40,426
Or maybe I've grown used to being scared.

298
00:20:42,303 --> 00:20:43,596
That hand…

299
00:20:43,680 --> 00:20:46,266
It's nothing.
It'll be alright in a second.

300
00:20:47,100 --> 00:20:51,145
You haven't changed at all.
Still living for someone else's dream.

301
00:20:55,858 --> 00:20:58,069
It's not like I don't understand.

302
00:21:00,613 --> 00:21:05,285
I don't think I'm scared
for myself anymore.

303
00:21:06,035 --> 00:21:07,412
I'm more scared that…

304
00:21:07,495 --> 00:21:08,913
Someday, you'll…

305
00:21:18,506 --> 00:21:21,718
Yes. I was able to recover
most of the data.

306
00:21:21,801 --> 00:21:25,054
The information on
one of the test subjects

307
00:21:25,138 --> 00:21:29,183
appears to be completely corrupted.

308
00:21:29,892 --> 00:21:32,770
I would say that it was
intentionally manipulated.

309
00:21:32,854 --> 00:21:34,314
There's no trace on the ICE.

310
00:21:34,397 --> 00:21:37,692
This hacking couldn't have been done
by an average runner.

311
00:21:39,902 --> 00:21:42,196
I don't believe Tanaka
would have erased it.

312
00:21:42,280 --> 00:21:46,117
So it must have been manipulated
during his capture.

313
00:21:47,035 --> 00:21:51,039
Understood.
I'll see what I can do to restore it.

314
00:21:51,122 --> 00:21:52,248
Goodbye.
